Package: frustumR
Title: GPU-Accelerated Scientific 3D Visualization
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R:
    person("Gilles", "Colling", role = c("aut", "cre"),
           email = "gilles@example.com")
Description: Create publication-quality 3D scientific figures using GPU
    acceleration. Supports isosurface extraction via marching cubes,
    point clouds, polylines, and triangle meshes. Built on Rust and wgpu
    for cross-platform deterministic output.
License: MIT + file LICENSE
URL: https://github.com/gcol33/frustumR
BugReports: https://github.com/gcol33/frustumR/issues
Encoding: UTF-8
Roxygen: list(markdown = TRUE)
RoxygenNote: 7.3.2
SystemRequirements: Cargo (Rust's package manager), rustc >= 1.70
Config/rextendr/version: 0.3.1
